+## Shared download artifacts
+
+When Chromium and its OpenClaw controller run in separate containers on the same
+host, operators can mount a dedicated artifact directory at the same absolute
+path in both containers and set `OPENCLAW_BROWSER_SHARED_ARTIFACTS_DIR` on the
+controller. This directory must already exist and must not be a symlink. Keep
+profiles, credentials, configuration, and the Gateway workspace outside it.
+
+Playwright uses a separate directory for each connection. Downloads are read with
+the native 10 MiB file limit and reject symlinks, hardlinks, and paths outside the
+shared root before entering ordinary browser output and node-proxy handling.
+Consumed artifacts are removed; disconnect and connection failure remove their
+connection directory. Operators must bound the shared storage and discard it
+after an unclean controller exit. This transport requires a shared filesystem;
+it does not transfer artifacts from arbitrary hosted CDP providers.
+
+Upload transport is unchanged: stage selected files in the managed upload or
+inbound media directory. The node proxy transfers their bytes without mounting
+the Gateway workspace into the browser.
+
